247-248-249-250	133,1389,596,2094	247. Flower, &c. of Wild Columbine. 248. A petal. 249. The 5 pods opening. 250. A separate pod.	A Wild Columbine stem (247) with lobed leaves, one open nodding flower and a bud; at left a single spurred petal (248); below, the five pods opening (249, right) and one separate pod (250, left).
251	686,846,1087,1363	251. Flower of Larkspur No. 6.	A Larkspur flower seen from the front, its spreading petal-like sepals round the small central petals, with the long spur of the upper sepal rising behind.
252	614,1386,1187,2097	252. Its sepals and petals displayed.	The same Larkspur flower taken apart and laid out: the spurred upper sepal at the top, four other broad sepals around, and the four small petals between them.
253	230,908,569,1113	253. Four petals of Larkspur No. 1, united into one body.	The single-bodied corolla of the field Larkspur seen from the side, its united petals ending behind in a long, slender, curving spur.
254	1337,863,1602,1385	254. Flower of Aconite.	An Aconite flower seen from the front, the tall hood or helmet at the top over a cluster of many stamens, with the lower sepals spreading below.
255	1220,1327,1742,2092	255. Its parts displayed: s, the sepals; p, the petals; st, stamens and pistils on the flower-stalk.	The Aconite flower taken apart: the hood-shaped upper sepal at top, the two long-clawed petals beneath it, the other sepals around, and the stamens and pistils on their stalk in the middle.
